  "details": "Currently, object.destroy will not destroy a gameobject passed in via a noodle.  The workaround at the moment is to create an object variable and then assign it the gameobject you wish to destroy. Then get that variable and pass that into object.destroy with a noodle. You also cannot directly convert the gameobject to an object through a convert node.",
